            <ArticleTitle>Mayaro virus infection, Amazon Basin region, Peru, 2010-2013.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1839-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3201/eid1911.130777</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>During 2010-2013, we recruited 16 persons with confirmed Mayaro virus infection in the Peruvian Amazon to prospectively follow clinical symptoms and serologic response over a 12-month period. Mayaro virus infection caused long-term arthralgia in more than half, similar to reports of other arthritogenic alphaviruses.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
